s morning at Midtown and Riverside. I know how stressful it is to have a full waiting room and no access to Dentrix, and I'm sorry for the impact this had on your team and your patients.\n\nHere's a quick summary of what happened and what we did:\n\n**What happened:** The security certificate on your HQ firewall expired overnight, which broke the secure network connections between Midtown, Riverside, and your main office. This is why front desk staff at those two locations couldn't reach the Dentrix database, while the main office was unaffected.\n\n**What we did:** As soon as you called at 8:47 AM, our team identified the cause within minutes and immediately began issuing a new certificate. Once received, we installed it and restored the connections. Riverside was confirmed working by 10:12 AM and Midtown by 10:15 AM — full resolution within about 90 minutes of your call.\n\n**Patient data:** To reassure you and your team — no patient records were lost or at risk. The Dentrix server itself was never down; the branch offices simply lost their secure path to reach it.\n\n**What we're doing to prevent this from happening again:** This certificate had been flagged in a prior review, and we're taking ownership of that gap. We're adding automated monitoring and alerting for certificate expiration dates on your network equipment so this type of issue is caught and resolved well before it can affect your operations.\n\nWe take outages like this seriously, especially when they affect patient care, and we appreciate your patience while we worked through it. Please don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or if you're seeing any lingering issues at either location.\n\nThank you,\n[Your Name]\n[Company Name] — Service Desk","ttft_ms":7784,"type":"result","duration_ms":7829,"uuid":"510be342-7f0b-4d37-aec6-3c83cf3bd026","ttft_stream_ms":761,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":761,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
